# Live capture: VM/370 R6 (VM/CE 1.2) under Hercules, recorded 2026-08-17.
#
# Script: packages/cli/scripts/record-vm.txt. This capture REACHES CMS: it logs on,
# IPLs CMS, gets "Ready;", has QUERY TERMINAL answered by CMS itself
# ("AUTOCR OFF, MORE 050 010, HOLD ON, TIMESTAMP OFF"), and logs off cleanly.
# 77 commands, 0 errors, 0 program checks.
#
# This replaces an earlier capture that stalled at CP READ. That one was taken
# before the logon sequence was fixed: the script typed LOGON as its first input,
# which the connect-time dismissal screen consumed and discarded, so the password
# arrived at a fresh CP READ as a command and CP answered "restart". See
# docs/live-testing.md, "The logon sequence", for the full explanation.
#
# REDACTED: one sent record containing the account password has been replaced with
# a comment line. The fixture is therefore replay-faithful only up to the password
# prompt; screens after it reflect a session where those bytes are absent. That is
# deliberate: a working password must never enter git history. Verified zero
# occurrences of the password's EBCDIC bytes remain.
#
# Note the password happens to equal the userid on this system, so the same EBCDIC
# byte sequence also appears legitimately inside the "LOGON CMSUSER" command and the
# host's echo of it. Those occurrences are the userid, which is not secret and is
# already in the script; only the bare-password record was redacted.
#
# What this capture exercises that the old one could not: the VM READ state, the
# CMS IPL, disk-access messages, a MORE... pause released by Clear, and a CMS
# command with a CMS reply.
